  "notes": "TIME OF DAY:\n{明|あ}け{方|がた} refers specifically to the period just before sunrise when the sky begins to lighten, typically between 4:00-6:00 AM depending on the season.\n\nRELATED TIME WORDS:\n- ⟦{夜明|よあ}け→夜明け：03655_yoake⟧ (dawn, daybreak - similar meaning)\n- ⟦{日|ひ}の{出|で}→日の出：17596_hinode⟧ (sunrise - the moment the sun appears)\n- ⟦{早朝|そうちょう}→早朝：03109_souchou⟧ (early morning)\n- ⟦{朝方|あさがた}→朝方：21392_asagata⟧ (toward morning)\n\nFORMS:\n⟦{明|あ}ける→明ける：21288_akeru⟧ (to dawn) + {方|がた} (time period suffix) → the time when it dawns",
